---
description: Keep the firmware modular and prevent god objects
alwaysApply: true
---

# Architecture boundaries

- Do not let a single type, module, or source file accumulate unrelated
  responsibilities. Keep transport/protocol validation, application state,
  hardware access, and UI rendering separate.
- Refactor before a component becomes a god object: extract a cohesive layer
  or focused type when it owns more than one domain concern or when its public
  API starts mixing them.
- Prefer small explicit interfaces at layer boundaries. The Rust/C FFI facade
  remains narrow: Rust owns protocol and state; C owns ESP-IDF and LVGL.
- Do not introduce speculative layers. Split only around real responsibilities
  and keep each extracted unit independently testable where practical.
